THOUGHT: `clsp` is a nullable field lazily initialized in `initClassPath()`. `getClsp()` currently returns it directly with a non-null return type, causing the NullAway error. The safest fix is to ensure callers either initialize the classpath first or get a clear failure if they don’t. I’ll change `getClsp()` to throw a `JadxRuntimeException` if `clsp` is still null, preserving the non-null contract without changing annotations. Then I’ll run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '496,499c\ 		public ClspGraph getClsp() {
			ClspGraph clspGraph = this.clsp;
			if (clspGraph == null) {
				throw new JadxRuntimeException("Class path not initialized, call initClassPath() first");
			}
			return clspGraph;
		}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/nodes/RootNode.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

